# ── LLM Relay ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent solving (`npm run agent:run`) and the dormant rule-proposal experiment
# route through llm-relay; human tests never call a model. No provider API keys
# live in this repo — the relay manages them. Paid models need a BYO key (below).
# Default for this app since 2026-08-27: the developer's own Codex sign-in,
# through the relay's localhost harness bridge. It needs the LOCAL relay and the
# bridge to be running, so the base URL below is the local one.
RELAY_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787/v1
RELAY_PROVIDER=codex
# `default` runs whatever Codex itself defaults to in the bridge's mode, so a
# new model needs no edit here (gpt-6-astra on 2026-10-01). The bridge reports
# the model that answered and `agent:run` records that one, never "default".
# A named slug pins a model instead, e.g. gpt-5.6-sol for the 2026-09-30 probe.
RELAY_MODEL=default
# Harness providers take reasoning effort as a request body field, not a header.
# It changes the answers enough that a run records the value it used, and two
# runs at different efforts are not comparable.
RELAY_EFFORT=high
# Required for the codex/claude-code default: agent:run is server-side, so it
# sends no browser Origin, and the relay now serves its harness providers to an
# originless caller only when the request carries the relay's LOCAL_API_KEY as
# X-Harness-Caller-Token (relay change 2026-10-03). Set this to the LOCAL_API_KEY
# in ~/Desktop/llm-relay/.dev.vars, or every agent:run is a 403
# harness_origin_forbidden. Not needed on the hosted openrouter alternative below.
RELAY_HARNESS_CALLER_TOKEN=

# Hosted alternative, no local bridge needed. The agent's image channel needs a
# vision model; this is the strong model the recorded probes in data/attempts/
# used (the weak control is google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite). Needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# RELAY_BASE_URL=https://llm-relay.ebarakos.workers.dev/v1
# RELAY_PROVIDER=openrouter
# RELAY_MODEL=google/gemini-3.5-flash

# Development experiment only: allow an LLM to propose a strict bounded rule.
# Pure code still constructs and validates the puzzle; the normal quiz route
# never uses this path.
# ENABLE_LLM_RULE_PROPOSALS=1

# The visual-family pilot gallery is available automatically in development.
# Set this only when deliberately exposing that surface in a production-like run.
# ENABLE_SCENE_PROTOTYPES=1

# ── Withdrawing a question family ────────────────────────────────────
# Families are public as soon as they pass the code checks, so this list is the
# way to pull one back out after a human pilot shows it confuses people. Give
# the family ids separated by commas. The list is read when the server starts:
# locally that means a restart; on Vercel an environment-variable change only
# reaches a new deployment, so redeploy after changing it. The server refuses to
# start if the list leaves too few families to build either test length. An id
# that matches no registered family withdraws nothing and only logs a warning,
# so check the spelling. A long test needs ten distinct families and the
# registry serves eleven, so only a constraint-spatial family (the one band with
# a family to spare) can be withdrawn on its own; withdrawing any other family
# stops the server until a family is added.
# WITHDRAWN_FAMILY_IDS=combining-machine-v1

# ── BYO provider keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for PAID models (e.g. the openrouter alternative above). Forwarded as
# X-User-Api-Key, which also bypasses the relay's shared rate limit.
# Put real keys in .env.local only — NEVER commit them.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Quiz scoring ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required in production. Use a stable random value of at least 32 characters.
# It encrypts and authenticates answer keys in the opaque quiz token sent to the browser.
# On Vercel, `npm run vercel:setup` creates and stores this automatically for
# production and preview. Do not copy the generated value into this repository.
# QUIZ_TOKEN_SECRET=
